<title>MEXICO: GSyR signs restructuring agreement.</title>
<headline>GSyR signs restructuring agreement.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Troubled Mexican retail chain Grupo Salinas y Rocha (GSyR) said on Thursday it had signed a memorandum of understanding to formalize debt restructuring with creditor banks.</p>
<p>GSyR expected to conclude restructuring of its debt, which totals some $500 million, over the coming weeks, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Grupo Financiero Serfin, Grupo Financiero Bancomer, Banco Santander Mexicano and Confia are Grupo Salinas y Rocha's main creditor banks.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
